{"title":"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The mean (average) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the smallest of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/39686bb86de3da59e5c2ff3f5d8065ff237843dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest number. Because the numbers are consecutive, the numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a186a5fd4879b180d5d4f42ddeb6bec9af98478b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2e1d87b1d3aefe9596c2581cda95f088aee03a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b4c3e97b90e7ed8f39e9634f062b3abc343052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The average/mean of these numbers would be the sum divided by the number of numbers, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/24176a7a69e115bd921a41ed5d9f408c04baa09c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x + x + 1 + x + 2 + x + 3 + x + 4}{5} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"305\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7da04a27ddaf7cb6e51472e4cd16e6382ac813c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x + 10}{5} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9960067d13626a8b9c07ecaa18c078d60a745ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f84d12c78a260a980ba6375e547eec40c65c2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 9 - 2 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"157\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the middle number. Because the numbers are consecutive, the numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffc131d8b736f8faba00e9c6227958a93e76cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b0495af1d7b094561fcade343847d464778c925d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a186a5fd4879b180d5d4f42ddeb6bec9af98478b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. We also realize that the mean must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> since all of the constant terms cancel out and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a7a2005b67ab81ee5ff231b2f370f1d71ebe1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. The smallest number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b380c59c9261efe62bca30b00e472110170c09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2 = 9 - 2 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"189\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley\">2010 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_C